\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Lattice formulae are a comparison}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{\citef{gurlebeck2002potentials} states that a Borel–Pompeiu
formula can be formulated for finite-difference potentials on a
uniform lattice. \citef{legatiuk2018borel} presents a discrete
Borel–Pompeiu formula on a rectangular lattice. The identity of
\ref{fdip-00P7} is the counting pairing on the periodic cubical
torus, and the harmonic term #{HF} remains in the formula.}
